From b7e8379930d4c94e82783330e668b83d6130e26a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: memra-lane <lane@localhost>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:09:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv4): the small-kernel diet takes every row count, one
 block per row

The fused HC finish and Q-LoRA norm/pack ran only on t=1 steps, so a
DSpark server, which runs its target on T=6 verify rows, kept five
unfused launches per layer site. Both fused kernels now index their row
by blockIdx.x, as the unfused kernels do, and the dispatch drops t == 1.
tests/dsv4_small_diet_gpu.rs adds multi-row cases (2, 6, 7, 16, 17, 64
rows, one magnitude range per row) that require each row to equal the
unfused multi-row chain and the same row launched alone.

Signed-off-by: memra-lane <lane@localhost>
